Phase 1 - Data Models (Mongoose Schemas):
  ✔ User schema - fullName, email, password, role (Lister/Seeker) @done(26-08-15)
  ✔ Listing schema - location, price, roomsAvailable, description, owner (ref User), availability status @done(26-08-15)
  ✔ InterestRequest schema - listing (ref), seeker (ref), status (pending/accepted/declined) @done(26-08-15)
  ✔ Add schema-level validation (email format, required fields, price > 0) @done(26-08-15)
  ☐ Add indexes where useful (e.g. listing location/price for search)

Phase 2 - Authentication:
  ✔ POST /auth/register - hash password with bcrypt, create user @done(26-08-16)
  ✔ POST /auth/login - verify password, issue JWT @done(26-08-16)
  ✔ JWT auth middleware (verify token, attach user to request) @done(26-08-16)
  ✔ Role-based access middleware (Lister vs Seeker) @done(26-08-16)
  ✔ Protect routes that require auth @done(26-08-16)

Phase 3 - Listings CRUD (Lister):
  ✔ POST /listings - create listing (Lister only) @done(26-08-16)
  ✔ GET /listings - browse/list all listings @done(26-08-16)
  ✔ GET /listings/:id - get single listing @done(26-08-16)
  ✔ PUT /listings/:id - update own listing only @done(26-08-16)
  ✔ DELETE /listings/:id - delete own listing only @done(26-08-16)
    ✔ Block deletion if listing has any accepted interest requests @done(26-08-16)
  ☐ Enforce "cannot manage other listers' listings" check

Phase 4 - Interest Requests:
  ☐ POST /listings/:id/requests - Seeker sends interest request
    ☐ Block duplicate requests (same seeker + same listing)
    ☐ Block listers from requesting their own listing
  ☐ GET /requests/mine - Seeker views own request history
  ☐ DELETE /requests/:id - Seeker cancels own pending request
  ☐ GET /listings/:id/requests - Lister views requests on their listing
  ☐ PATCH /requests/:id/accept - Lister accepts (owner-only check)
  ☐ PATCH /requests/:id/decline - Lister declines (owner-only check)
  ☐ Confirm accepting one request does NOT auto-decline others

